{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 36, :comments ["<b>It is a solemn assembly.</b> I detain you with Me — like a king who invited his sons to a feast for so many days; when the time came to send them off, he said: My children, I ask of you, stay with me one more day — your departure is hard for me." "<b>Any laborious work.</b> Even work that is a service for you — such that if you do not do it, there is a loss of money in the matter." "<b>You shall not do.</b> One might think the intermediate days of the Festival are also forbidden in laborious work — Scripture says ״הוּא״ (there)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:08:01.273608451Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}